// crt's constants. A project that carries crt as a subdirectory -- every
// project tools/c2id.sh generates, and tests/crt's -- has this file at its own
// root instead, because conf.id is only read at a root.
//
// wzero: the literal 0, as a word. Two reasons it exists rather than a bare `0`:
//
//   * a list literal takes its element type from its *first* element, so
//     `[0, 0]` is an `int[]` and will not initialise a `word[]`;
//   * every *later* element must be word-typed too. idc.py's list literal is
//     a C varargs call whose cells are read as `long long`, and it does not
//     insert a widening cast for a `word`-typed element -- so an `int`
//     expression in a `word[]` literal is read back with 32 bits of garbage
//     on top. Callers of c_format must build their argument lists the same
//     way: every element already a `word`.
word wzero = 0;
